N2  - Abstract The regulation of learning, including self-regulated learning (SRL) and socially shared regulation of learning (SSRL), is a key skill that should already be practiced in primary education. The shift toward student-centered, collaborative, and open-ended processes, such as phenomenon-based learning, increases the need for pupils to take charge of their own learning. However, due to the varying abilities of primary school pupils to regulate their learning, such processes can be challengin
